{"id":"000VZW","title":"Fireflines: Hit the Lights","author":"dawsonjones2020","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-11T15:20:29+00:00","posted":"Heute, 14:00 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle is the second in a series exploring the firefly ruleset. I hope you enjoy! If you do, feel free to leave a comment and check out my other puzzles!\n\nSolve on SudokuPad\n\nRules\n\nSudoku: Each row, column, and 3×3 box contains the digits 1–9 once each.\n\nFirefly: From each white circle, draw a line to another circle (possibly itself) to create a connected network. Lines must start at the attached black dot, move horizontally or vertically between cell centers and cannot branch or overlap, go through other circles or connect between two black dots. A digit in a circle indicates the number of turns its line makes.\n\nHit Count: Firefly paths form a hitline. The ending circle is NOT on the hitline. Digits may not repeat on a hitline. The digit in the starting circle indicates how many digits match their position number along that line, starting at the circled digit (which is 'position 1').\n\nIf you're not familiar with the firefly rules and would like some examples click here","solutionCode":"Row 9.","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/1jj6uifois","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/1jj6uifois","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-11T15:20:29+00:00"}